    "updated_at": "2023-10-11T04:03:45Z",
    "body": "Ok, I see, thanks for your response.\r\n\r\nI don't know enough about bluetooth low energy to ask the right questions but I'll play around with it to see if there is a reliable mechanism for linking devices to users when there is many potential device GUID advertising in a given space, so that a user's device can reliably be used to track indoor positioning, without needing to re-register or calibrate once a user opts in and registers a device for the first time. Should I be looking at UWB for indoor positioning? I would think it's not nearly ubiquitous enough for my use case where the users bring their own devices. Thanks for your time.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
